          ```
        
        * **Theme Color Variables:**
          DaisyUI themes provide CSS variables for consistent color usage:
          - `--p`: Primary color
          - `--s`: Secondary color
          - `--a`: Accent color
          - `--n`: Neutral color
          - `--b1`, `--b2`, `--b3`: Base colors (background)
          - `--bc`: Base content color (text)
          - `--in`: Info color
          - `--su`: Success color
          - `--wa`: Warning color
          - `--er`: Error color
          
          Usage:
          ```jsx
          <div style={{ backgroundColor: 'var(--p)', color: 'var(--pc)' }}>
            This div uses the primary color with appropriate contrast text
          </div>
          ```
        
        * **Responsive Theming:**
          - Combine with media queries for automatic light/dark modes:
          ```css
          @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
            html {
              data-theme: "dark";
            }
          }
          ```

48. **Color Usage Best Practices:**
    *   **Instruction:** Follow a consistent pattern for color usage with DaisyUI's semantic color system. IMPORTANT: for development, we want everything to be greyscale to simplify decisions. Do not use any non-greyscale colors.
    *   **Guideline:**
        * **Semantic Color Usage:**
          - `primary`: Main brand color, used for primary actions and key UI elements
          - `secondary`: Complementary color, used for secondary actions and less prominent elements
          - `accent`: Highlight color, used sparingly for emphasis
          - `neutral`: Neutral color, used for text, backgrounds, and UI elements
          - `base`: Background color for the page/components
          - `info`: Informational elements (blue)
          - `success`: Success states/actions (green)
          - `warning`: Warning states/actions (yellow/orange)
          - `error`: Error states/destructive actions (red)
        
        * **Color Application Examples:**
          ```jsx
          {/* Primary actions */}
          <button className="btn btn-primary">Save Changes</button>
          
          {/* Secondary actions */}
          <button className="btn btn-secondary">View Details</button>
          
          {/* Destructive actions */}
          <button className="btn btn-error">Delete Account</button>
          
          {/* Status indicators */}
          <div className="badge badge-success">Active</div>
          <div className="badge badge-warning">Pending</div>
          <div className="badge badge-error">Failed</div>
          
          {/* Alerts and notifications */}
          <div className="alert alert-info">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" className="stroke-current shrink-0 w-6 h-6"><path strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round" strokeWidth="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
            <span>New software update available.</span>
          </div>
          ```
